A||||3||Gokart||What to do?!?||||5
Z||000000||Gokart||10-28-1999||07:51 PM||||I want to do the right thing for my GT when I take it off the road for the winter and you've all been so helpful, especially theogre, thank you. But now I get a very good mechanic telling me that if I don't plan on driving my GT, which I don't, not to even start it at all. He says I could do more damage than good by starting it every so often. He told me to buy some engine fogger, mostly used on boats, spray it in the air intake and just let'er sit till spring. What do any of you think of this? Ever heard of this engine fogger?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||10-28-1999||08:35 PM||||I know why he's likely telling you that.... allot of people start the thing then don't run it long enough. You have to run it to full operating temp and keep it there for a while. like 30-60 minutes.<P>I've heard of what he's telling you. never used it.<P>The main thing I've seen fail on cars that are parked for a long time is the water pump. They usually don't fail right away after you start driving, but more like a month or so latter. It's nearly always seal failure. I think a bit of rust builds up next to the seal and then eats it up in fairly short order.<P>The rest of the motor does fine as long as you put Stabil in the gas. Stabil prevents the things that happen as fuel evaporates. This isn't as big a problem maybe with EFI, but I'd still use it. Stabil is cheap. Fill the gas tank before storing. it prevents the tank drawing watter.<P>I'd keep it so you can drive it on good days. take it out and run it for an hour or so. you know you don't really want to park it for months straight anyway.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Driving it with the stabil in won't hurt it at all.||||reg||1
Z||000002||four50four||10-28-1999||09:07 PM||||I've used fogging oil before, its for snowmobiles and boats. you just start the engine, and spray it in till the exhaust gets real smokey. it gets inside the engine and thouroughly lubricates everything. It is a must for storing 2-stroke engines, not sure about cars though||||reg||3
Z||000003||Gokart||10-29-1999||04:06 AM||||Thanks again Ogre. I'm going with your advice, case closed! I was kind of foggy about this mechanics tip anyway!!||||reg||14
